### REST Client Test File for Contact CRUD Operations
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080
### Security: userId is extracted from JWT, never from the URL.
### Use the seeded users: test@gmail.com / admin@gmail.com (password: 123456)

### ============================================
### SETUP: Login to get tokens
### ============================================

### 0a. Login as USER (test@gmail.com)
# @name loginUser
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "test@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 0b. Login as ADMIN (admin@gmail.com)
# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "admin@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### ============================================
### SUCCESS CASES (as USER)
### ============================================

### 1. Create Contact - Success
# @name createContact
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Juan Perez",
    "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
    "phone": "1123456789"
}

### 2. List My Contacts - Success
# @name listMyContacts
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 3. Get Contact By Id - Success
# @name getContactById
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 4. Update Contact - Success
# @name updateContact
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Juan Perez Actualizado",
    "email": "juan.nuevo@example.com",
    "phone": "1199999999"
}

### 5. Delete Contact - Success
# @name deleteContact
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 6. Get Deleted Contact - Not Found (404)
# @name getDeletedContact
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ============================================
### ADMIN CASES
### ============================================

### 7. List ALL Contacts - as ADMIN
# @name listAllAsAdmin
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ============================================
### ERROR CASES
### ============================================

### 8. Create Contact - Missing name (400)
# @name createContactNoName
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "sinnombre@example.com",
    "phone": "1123456789"
}

### 9. Create Contact - Invalid email (400)
# @name createContactBadEmail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Juan",
    "email": "esto-no-es-un-email",
    "phone": "1123456789"
}

### 10. Create Contact - Duplicate email (409)
# @name createContactDuplicate
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Otra Persona",
    "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
    "phone": "1188888888"
}

### 11. Get Contact - Malformed Id (400)
# @name getContactBadId
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/esto-no-es-un-numero
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 12. Get Contact - No Token (401)
# @name getContactNoToken
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/1

### 13. Get Contact - Non-existent Id (404)
# @name getContactNonExistent
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/contacts/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.data.accessToken}}